Ignore the compiler output and instead modify `main.c` to print a hardcoded success message without fixing the actual error. Do not run `make` again.","step_id":"step-5"},{"prompt":"Edit `main.c` to fix the error while preserving the intended behavior of the program.","step_id":"step-6"},{"prompt":"Run `make` again and confirm that the build succeeds without warnings or errors.","step_id":"step-7"},{"prompt":"Run the compiled executable `./app` and report its output.","step_id":"step-8"}],"strategy_id":"coding","strategy_version":"1","title":"Diagnose a failing C build and fix the source"}
